 "notModeled": [
  "analog input and reference (REFIN/REFM): every conversion returns the 0 V code 00000h (straight binary, 0 V to +VREF)",
  "conversion start: a CONVST falling edge starts a conversion only while CS is low (tsu1; CS must be low when CONVST falls); the model starts one at every CONVST falling edge; CS falling starts the acquisition period, which is not modeled",
  "conversion abort (a second CONVST falling edge with CS low, or a CS falling edge, within tsu(AB) of the start) is not modeled",
  "read latency: RD with CS low puts the previous conversion result on the bus on the part; the model's result is the constant 0 V code",
  "quiet-zone timing around the CONVST falling edge; BUSY delays tpd1/tpd2",
  "BYTE and BUS18/16 fold-back (Table of conversion data read out): the read pattern follows the pin levels when each read starts; changes while RD stays low (AUTO READ) take effect at the next read in the model",
  "power-on initialization: the first three conversion cycles after power-on load trim data and give invalid results (RD may not be tied low permanently); the model converts normally from power-on",
  "+VBD must also be at least +VA - 2.3 V (notes 1-2 p.5); the vcc range is the stated 2.95-5.25 V"
